 "nl": [
  "dns-servers is isolated: it may only reach hr on syslog (UDP 514); dmz-web on HTTPS (TCP 443), and nothing else.",
  "Hosts in hr may reach dns-servers over syslog (UDP 514) and DNS over UDP 53 and NTP (UDP 123).",
  "dns-servers must never reach printers, regardless of any other rule.",
  "Block SNMP (UDP 161) from dmz-web to dns-servers; the rest of any UDP port between them is allowed.",
  "library must never reach guest-wifi, regardless of any other rule.",
  "Hosts in printers may reach library over SNMP (UDP 161) and RTSP (TCP 554) and IMAP (TCP 143).",
  "Deny all traffic from hr to library (this overrides any public service).",
  "printers offers HTTP (TCP 80) and NTP (UDP 123) to every zone.",
  "Hosts in guest-wifi may reach dmz-web over SSH (TCP 22) and syslog (UDP 514) and NTP (UDP 123).",
  "guest-wifi offers HTTP (TCP 80) to every zone.",
  "Any zone may connect to guest-wifi over NTP (UDP 123) and DNS over UDP 53.",
  "Any zone may connect to hr over HTTP (TCP 80) and HTTPS (TCP 443).",
  "Hosts in hr may reach guest-wifi over RTSP (TCP 554) and HTTP (TCP 80) and HTTPS (TCP 443).",
  "dns-servers must accept RDP (TCP 3389) and LDAP (TCP 389) and IMAP (TCP 143) from guest-wifi.",
  "Allow guest-wifi to connect to hr using syslog (UDP 514) and RDP (TCP 3389).",
  "Hosts in library may reach printers over PostgreSQL (TCP 5432).",
  "Allow guest-wifi to connect to dmz-web using PostgreSQL (TCP 5432) and SMTP (TCP 25) and IMAP (TCP 143).",
  "Any zone may connect to library over HTTPS (TCP 443) and DNS over UDP 53.",
  "Any zone may connect to dmz-web over HTTP (TCP 80).",
  "dns-servers must accept NTP (UDP 123) and syslog (UDP 514) from hr.",
  "guest-wifi may use any UDP port towards dmz-web, except SNMP (UDP 161), TFTP (UDP 69), which must be blocked.",
  "Hosts in dns-servers may reach library over SSH (TCP 22) and NTP (UDP 123) and HTTP (TCP 80).",
  "hr must accept RTSP (TCP 554) from dmz-web.",
  "Hosts in dns-servers may reach dmz-web over SSH (TCP 22) and SMB (TCP 445) and RTSP (TCP 554).",
  "Hosts in library may reach dmz-web over SMB (TCP 445) and HTTP (TCP 80) and IMAP (TCP 143).",
  "Make DNS over UDP 53 and HTTP (TCP 80) on dmz-web reachable from all internal zones.",
  "No packet from library may enter printers, even for services open to everyone.",
  "guest-wifi must accept LDAP (TCP 389) and IMAP (TCP 143) from dns-servers.",
  "hr must accept SSH (TCP 22) and SMB (TCP 445) and RDP (TCP 3389) from dns-servers."
 ],
